1
00:00:01,120 --> 00:00:03,920
Most AI agents can solve a task today.

2
00:00:03,950 --> 00:00:07,860
But when they get something wrong, a bad assumption, the wrong tool,

3
00:00:07,890 --> 00:00:10,210
does any of that carry over to tomorrow?

4
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:11,420
Usually not.

5
00:00:11,450 --> 00:00:13,670
Every session starts from zero.

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,480
This is RecallIQ.

7
00:00:16,510 --> 00:00:20,690
It's an AI agent that investigates real Sui Mainnet activity through Tatum,

8
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:22,543
checks every claim against fresh chain data,

9
00:00:22,573 --> 00:00:24,810
and keeps what it learns in Walrus Memory.

10
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:26,830
So the next session starts smarter.

11
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:30,180
Let's ask it something new:

12
00:00:30,210 --> 00:00:32,230
what has this address been doing?

13
00:00:32,260 --> 00:00:35,740
First, it recalls six relevant lessons from Walrus.

14
00:00:35,770 --> 00:00:39,530
Then WorthIt picks the tools, free Tatum tools first.

15
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:44,270
Every call reads live Sui data through Tatum's gRPC gateway,

16
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:46,690
and everything it reads becomes evidence.

17
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:48,370
When the agent reports back,

18
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:51,360
each claim is re-checked against a fresh chain read.

19
00:00:51,390 --> 00:00:53,070
All five verified.

20
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:56,400
And here's why it worked that way:

21
00:00:56,430 --> 00:01:00,910
the lessons it applied, each one recalled from a Walrus blob.

22
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:04,320
One of them came from a real mistake.

23
00:01:04,350 --> 00:01:07,450
A few days earlier, in another session,

24
00:01:07,480 --> 00:01:09,960
the agent asserted a gas amount with the wrong sign,

25
00:01:09,990 --> 00:01:11,940
and the chain contradicted it.

26
00:01:11,970 --> 00:01:17,100
The Agent Autopsy diagnosed an unsupported claim and turned it into a rule:

27
00:01:17,130 --> 00:01:20,870
every fact needs evidence and a checkable assertion.

28
00:01:21,940 --> 00:01:24,500
That lesson was written to Walrus Mainnet.

29
00:01:24,530 --> 00:01:29,530
Here's the exact text it stored, and here's its blob, on Walruscan.

30
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:34,510
Later that day, a completely different question.

31
00:01:34,540 --> 00:01:39,720
RecallIQ brought that lesson back from Walrus, and it isn't just context,

32
00:01:39,750 --> 00:01:41,500
it's an enforced policy.

33
00:01:41,530 --> 00:01:45,880
The agent's first report was rejected because three claims lacked evidence.

34
00:01:45,910 --> 00:01:48,970
The agent fixed them, and all four verified.

35
00:01:51,540 --> 00:01:53,480
WorthIt decides what's worth paying for.

36
00:01:53,510 --> 00:01:57,370
It ranks tools by relevance and by reliability measured on real runs.

37
00:01:57,400 --> 00:02:01,820
A paid specialist is only offered when its expected benefit clears the bar.

38
00:02:01,850 --> 00:02:03,510
Here it didn't, so nothing was spent.

39
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:05,044
When one is worth it,

40
00:02:05,074 --> 00:02:08,350
you approve the exact x402 payment on Sui in your own wallet,

41
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:12,370
and RecallIQ confirms the settlement on chain before using the result.

42
00:02:14,780 --> 00:02:17,040
The Learning Lab traces every lesson,

43
00:02:17,070 --> 00:02:20,560
from the failure that created it to the decisions it changed.

44
00:02:20,590 --> 00:02:24,930
RecallIQ brings persistent memory, verified blockchain data,

45
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:27,620
and cost-aware decisions into one agent.

46
00:02:27,650 --> 00:02:32,090
Because software should learn from experience, not start over every time.
